feat: Add Agent Cluster Platform implementation

## Summary
Complete implementation of the Agent Cluster Platform feature, enabling users to:
- Define packs as agent clusters with metadata
- Create dynamic clusters from multiple packs at runtime
- Schedule tasks that run across agent groups
- Manage cluster lifecycle through API and UI

## Changes

### Backend
- `server/routes/clusters.js`: REST API endpoints (7 endpoints)
- `server/routes/clusters-db.js`: SQLite database persistence layer
- `server/cron-mcp.js`: Extended scheduling tools with cluster support
- `server.js`: Route registration for cluster APIs

### Frontend
- `web/src/components/clusters/ClusterComposerModal.tsx`: New component
- `web/src/pages/AgentsPage.tsx`: Added cluster listing
- `web/src/lib/packs-api.ts`: Added cluster API functions
- `web/src/locales/*/common.json`: i18n translations (EN + ZH)

### Core
- `lib/pack-manifest.js`: Cluster metadata validation
- `catalog.js`: Added cluster fields to catalog responses

### Testing & Docs
- `scripts/test-cluster-platform.mjs`: Unit test suite (8 tests)
- `docs/`: 6 documentation files created
- `AGENT_CLUSTER_README.md`: Project README
- `CHANGELOG.md`: Version history
- `DELIVERY_CHECKLIST.md`: Delivery verification

## Validation
- ✅ All 8 unit tests passing
- ✅ OpenSpec validation passed (8/8)
- ✅ No syntax errors
- ✅ Backward compatible

## Migration Notes
- Existing packs without cluster metadata continue to work unchanged
- Database file automatically created at `<data-dir>/clusters.db`
- No breaking changes to existing APIs

